# Test: with no ze running, validate starts no external plugin and says its section is not available
#
# Question: when `ze config validate` runs with no ze listening on a config
# that declares an external plugin and holds a section under that plugin's
# root, does it refuse the section, say that a running ze was asked and why
# none answered, and name `ze start` as the one fix, without starting the
# program the config names? And does it still accept a config that holds no
# such section, and a compiled-in plugin?
# Why not a unit test: TestValidateRouteFallsBackWhenNoDaemonListens proves the
# route over a stub ask. This proves the `ze` binary an operator runs: no
# route from the command line to a fork of the declared program, the real walk
# to a listener that is not there, and the message as it is printed.
#
# The declared program writes a marker file when it is started, in any mode,
# and then answers a declaration query the way a conforming plugin does. Under
# the behaviour the owner ruled out, validate ran it in declare mode, the
# marker appeared and the section was accepted. Step 4 is the control: the
# conformance checker, the one command that starts a named program with no
# daemon, starts the same program from the same directory, and its marker
# shows that a start leaves one where the test looks.
#
# Source of the contract (Thomas): "plugin command requiring external plugins
# which can not be started from the code when no daemon is running to pass it
# to are not available, for command built-in then yes you should run them as
# we can look them up in the yang hardcoded in the binary".
#
# This file asserted `show config validation ze.conf` and `fix: ze cli`. That
# advice fails: typed in a `ze cli` session, the daemon reads ze.conf on its
# own host through command.CallerPath, which admits its config directories
# only, never the operator's working directory. The command now passes the
# config to a running ze itself, and with none running the fix is to start one.
#
# ze.ssh.port points the ask at the runner's $PORT, where nothing listens, so
# another session's daemon on the default port cannot answer it.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-2 and AC-15 of spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup, as the
#   ruling restates them, and AC-19 and AC-21 of its phase 10.
# PREVENTS: inspecting a config someone else wrote running their command; a
#   bare "unknown top-level keyword" with no word about why; advice the daemon
#   then refuses; validate refusing every config that declares an external
#   plugin.
#
# The program is a script the run string hands to a shell by name, because a
# declaration holds double quotes and the config's run string is itself
# double-quoted. It carries no interpreter line and no command of this file
# starts a shell directly: TestNoPythonLeRemains (internal/le/contract_test.go)
# refuses a functional test that embeds either.

option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT

# Leaves a marker named after its first argument, then answers a declaration
# query.
tmpfs=marker.run:terminator=EOF_RUN
echo started > "started-$1.marker"
printf '%s\n' '#1 ze-plugin-engine:declare-registration {"protocol-version":1,"wants-config":["acme-shell"],"schemas":[{"module":"acme-shell-conf","namespace":"urn:acme:shell:conf","yang-text":"module acme-shell-conf { namespace \"urn:acme:shell:conf\"; prefix shell; container acme-shell { presence \"The acme shell plugin is configured\"; leaf greeting { type string { length \"1..64\"; } } } }"}]}'
EOF_RUN

tmpfs=ze.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external acme-shell {
		run "sh marker.run by-ze"
		encoder json
	}
}

acme-shell {
	greeting hello
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=no-section.conf:terminator=EOF_NO_SECTION
plugin {
	external acme-shell {
		run "sh marker.run by-ze"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_NO_SECTION

tmpfs=built-in.conf:terminator=EOF_BUILT_IN
plugin {
	internal static {
		use static
	}
}
EOF_BUILT_IN

# The section of the external plugin is refused: a running ze was asked, none
# listens, and the one fix starts one.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate ze.conf:exit=1
expect=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword: acme-shell
expect=stdout:contains=the config declares external plugin "acme-shell"
expect=stdout:contains=starts no plugin
expect=stdout:contains=none answered: no ze listens at 127.0.0.1:
expect=stdout:contains=then `ze config validate ze.conf` again
expect=stdout:contains=fix: ze start
reject=stdout:contains=show config validation
reject=stdout:contains=fix: ze cli

# A config that declares the plugin and holds no section of it is valid, with
# no ze running: nothing in it needs the plugin's schema.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate no-section.conf:exit=0
reject=stdout:contains=external plugin "acme-shell"
reject=stdout:contains=unknown top-level keyword

# A compiled-in plugin is judged with the schema in the binary, as before.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze config validate built-in.conf:exit=0

# Control: the conformance checker starts the program, with no daemon, and
# that start leaves its marker in this directory.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze show plugin conformance run "sh marker.run by-checker" name acme-shell:exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern=program-starts +declare +pass

expect=file:path=started-by-checker.marker:exists=true
expect=file:path=started-by-ze.marker:absent=true
